          "english": "Modern U.S. cities were designed to make exercise unnecessary. Cars and elevators once symbolized urban areas as machines for more efficient living. Now it is clear that these improvements provide great benefits but also __(26)__ health costs. Recent studies show that urban __(27)__ encourages more driving and is associated with heavier weight. This __(28)__ suggests that the layout and design of cities can hinder or promote healthier lifestyle choices and it is __(29)__ that urban planners bear this in mind.",
