          "number": 2,
          "letter": "B",
          "english": "To explore this possibility more deeply, let's look at some of the common misconceptions about dementia and the aging brain. First of all, dementia is not an inevitable part of the normal aging process. Most older adults do not develop Alzheimer's disease or other forms of dementia. It is also important to remember that dementia is not the same thing as normal forgetfulness. At any age, we might experience difficulty finding the exact word we want or have trouble remembering the name of the person we just met. People with dementia have more serious problems, like feeling confused or getting lost in a familiar place. Think of it this way: If you forget where you parked your car at the mall, that's normal; if you forget how to drive a car, that may be a signal that something more serious is going on.",
          "chinese": "为了更深入地探讨这种可能性，让我们看看一些关于痴呆症和老年人大脑的常见误解。首先，痴呆症并不是正常衰老过程中的必然组成部分。大多数老年人不会患上阿尔茨海默氏病或其他形式的痴呆症。还必须记住，痴呆症与正常的健忘并不是一回事。在任何年龄，我们都可能遇到难以找到想说的确切词语，或记不起刚刚认识的人的姓名的情况。痴呆症患者面临的问题更加严重，例如感到困惑，或在熟悉的地方迷路。可以这样理解：如果你忘了把车停在商场的什么地方，这属于正常情况；如果你忘了该如何开车，那可能说明正在发生更为严重的问题。",
